    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0277" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg243"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 343.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that your dispatch No.
                    283, of the 27th ultimo, inclosing copy of your note of the 26th ultimo to the
                    German foreign office relative to the alleged discrimination against woods of
                    American origin in the freight tariff upon railways in Germany under Government
                    control has been received.</p>
                <p>Your able presentation of the matter to the foreign office is fully approved by
                    the Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
